.* WRKMSGQ: the message queues a name selects, with their options.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=MSGQ CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=TEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=QUEUES VARS='OPT MSGQ LIB TEXT'.
:KEYL NAME=WRKKEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display names only
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Repeat position to
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Position to
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION=MOREKEYS.F24=More keys
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKMSGQ KEYL=WRKKEYS HELP=WRKMSGQH ENTER='RETURN 1'.Work with Message Queues
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=QUEUES ACTLEN=2 EXTACT=YES VIEWS=2 SCROLL=YES MAXHEAD=2.
:LISTACT OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='CMD ?CRTMSGQ MSGQ(&LIB./&MSGQ.)'.1=Create
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?CHGMSGQ MSGQ(&LIB./&MSGQ.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DLTMSGQ MSGQ(&LIB./&MSGQ.)'.4=Delete
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPMSG MSGQ(&LIB./&MSGQ.)'.5=Display messages
:LISTACT OPTION=14 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD CLRMSGQ MSGQ(&LIB./&MSGQ.)'.14=Clear
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=MSGQ USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES.Message Queue
:LISTCOL VAR=LIB USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES.Library
:LISTCOL VAR=TEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT MSGQ LIB TEXT'.
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT MSGQ LIB'.
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1, 2 and 5 or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKMSGQH.Work with Message Queues - Help
:P.The message queues the name selects, a row each. Type an option next
to a queue, or on the first line with a new name to create one, and
press Enter; a command typed on the command line runs as typed.
:P.F17 positions the list at the queue named on the command line, F16
does it again, F11 shows the names alone and F5 lists the queues again.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F3 and F12 leave the list. F4 prompts the command on the command
line, F9 brings the previous one back.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
